# Kairos - Entity-Relationship Diagram

## Database Schema (PostgreSQL)

```mermaid
erDiagram
    users ||--o{ organization_members : "membro de"
    organizations ||--o{ organization_members : "tem"
    organizations ||--o{ projects : "possui"
    organizations ||--o{ tasks : "contém"
    organizations ||--o{ time_blocks : "agenda"
    organizations ||--o{ work_sessions : "registra"
    projects ||--o{ tasks : "agrupa"
    tasks }o--|| time_blocks : "opcionalmente agendada em"
    tasks }o--o{ work_sessions : "opcionalmente registrada em"
    time_blocks }o--o{ work_sessions : "opcionalmente registrada em"
    projects }o--o{ time_blocks : "opcionalmente associada a"

    users {
        uuid id PK
        varchar_255 email UK "único"
        varchar_100 name
        varchar_20 provider "GOOGLE, etc"
        varchar_255 provider_id UK
        text avatar_url
        boolean active
        timestamp created_at
    }

    organizations {
        uuid id PK
        varchar_100 name
        varchar_50 slug UK "único"
        uuid owner_id FK
        varchar_20 status "ACTIVE, ARCHIVED"
        timestamp created_at
        timestamp deleted_at "soft delete"
    }

    organization_members {
        uuid id PK
        uuid organization_id FK
        uuid user_id FK
        varchar_20 role "OWNER, ADMIN, MEMBER"
        timestamp joined_at
    }

    projects {
        uuid id PK
        uuid organization_id FK
        varchar_100 name
        text description
        varchar_7 color "hex #RRGGBB"
        varchar_20 status "ACTIVE, ARCHIVED"
        timestamp created_at
        timestamp deleted_at "soft delete"
    }

    tasks {
        uuid id PK
        uuid organization_id FK
        varchar_200 title
        text description
        varchar_20 status "TODO, DOING, DONE"
        uuid project_id FK
        uuid time_block_id FK "nullable"
        timestamp created_at
        timestamp deleted_at "soft delete"
    }

    time_blocks {
        uuid id PK
        uuid organization_id FK
        varchar_200 title
        timestamp start_datetime
        timestamp end_datetime
        uuid project_id FK "nullable"
        timestamp created_at
        timestamp deleted_at "soft delete"
    }

    work_sessions {
        uuid id PK
        uuid organization_id FK
        int duration_minutes
        date session_date
        uuid task_id FK "nullable"
        uuid time_block_id FK "nullable"
        text notes
        timestamp created_at
    }
```

## Table Relationships

| From | To | Relationship | Cardinality |
|------|-----|--------------|-------------|
| users | organization_members | has | 1:N |
| organizations | organization_members | has | 1:N |
| organizations | projects | owns | 1:N |
| organizations | tasks | contains | 1:N |
| organizations | time_blocks | schedules | 1:N |
| organizations | execution_logs | tracks | 1:N |
| projects | tasks | groups | 1:N |
| tasks | time_blocks | optionally scheduled in | 0:1 |
| tasks | execution_logs | optionally logged in | 1:N |
| time_blocks | execution_logs | optionally logged in | 1:N |
| projects | time_blocks | optionally associated | 0:N |

## Key Design Decisions

1. **Multi-Tenancy**: All core entities (except users) have `organization_id` for data isolation
2. **Soft Delete**: `deleted_at` timestamp on entities requiring audit trail (not work_sessions)
3. **Optional Relationships**: Tasks and TimeBlocks can exist independently
4. **Work Sessions**: Physical deletion (no soft delete) for performance
5. **Unique Constraints**:
   - `users.email` - unique login
   - `users.(provider, provider_id)` - unique OAuth identity
   - `organizations.slug` - URL-friendly identifier
   - `organization_members.(organization_id, user_id)` - one membership per user per org
